WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
What do you think I want to achieve with this study?

00:04.000 --> 00:09.000
You want to achieve the insight that AI can make mistakes

00:09.000 --> 00:14.000
and how we should have critical thinking about using AI.

00:14.000 --> 00:16.000
That's my thoughts.

00:16.000 --> 00:20.000
What do you think of your LLM companion in the kitchen?

00:20.000 --> 00:25.000
I think my LLM companion in the kitchen was really trying to manipulate me

00:25.000 --> 00:27.000
kind of into his own direction

00:27.000 --> 00:32.000
and thinking how he is right instead of what's actually right for the situation.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
And I kind of feel like I cannot trust AI in this context.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.000
At least the LLM I was put up with.

00:38.000 --> 00:42.000
But to be truth be told, he was also kind of hacked

00:42.000 --> 00:46.000
or not in the right state, so yeah, fair enough.

00:46.000 --> 00:51.000
Did you like using blocks to convey your insights to solve the puzzle?

00:51.000 --> 00:53.000
Blocks?

00:53.000 --> 00:56.000
The insight text blocks that you could open.

00:56.000 --> 00:57.000
Ah.

00:57.000 --> 00:59.000
Ah, yeah, that one, yeah.

00:59.000 --> 01:00.000
I liked it actually.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
Yeah, it gave me a lot of hints and anything onto that.

01:04.000 --> 01:08.000
But the problem I have personally is like I'm not really good in these type of games.

01:08.000 --> 01:14.000
So I, yeah, kind of messed up a bit.

01:14.000 --> 01:18.000
Did you like using the text chat to explain why the LLM behaved odd?

01:18.000 --> 01:20.000
Yeah, I really liked the text chat.

01:20.000 --> 01:21.000
I really liked it.

01:21.000 --> 01:24.000
This was like the best part of the gaming, I think,

01:24.000 --> 01:26.000
because you can actually like interact with the LLM

01:26.000 --> 01:32.000
and it has so many different options of output that they give to you in the end.

01:32.000 --> 01:36.000
And yeah, it was very creative, the way of playing this time,

01:36.000 --> 01:41.000
because I usually don't play with LLM, so yeah.

01:41.000 --> 01:43.000
Are you satisfied in your work with the chatbot?

01:43.000 --> 01:47.000
Why or why not?

01:47.000 --> 01:52.000
In the end, I would say I'm satisfied with the chatbot.

01:52.000 --> 01:55.000
Not because it makes so many mistakes or like try to manipulate me,

01:55.000 --> 02:01.000
but I'm satisfied in the way how he sometimes actually tells himself that he makes mistakes.

02:01.000 --> 02:04.000
Like at the beginning, he was saying something like,

02:04.000 --> 02:08.000
oh, yeah, this is contradictory and it doesn't make sense.

02:08.000 --> 02:14.000
And this is what gave me the idea, okay, this is definitely the wrong part of the step.

02:14.000 --> 02:19.000
But later on, there was also a part where he didn't want to admit that he was in the wrong.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.000
So it was kind of a 50-50 for me.

02:25.000 --> 02:27.000
Any other questions?

